start: mr
R1: 3ch=dc 11dc@ring ss@top
R2: ch sc@same [{hdc 2ch hdc}@st 2sc]x3 {hdc 2ch hdc}@st sc ss@top fo
R3: {3dc 2ch 3dc}@sp [ch 4sk {3dc 2ch 3dc}@sp]x3 ch 4sk ss@top
R4: ch sc@same 2sc [{sc ch sc}@sp 3sc 5ch sk 3sc]x3 {sc ch sc}@sp 3sc 5ch sk ss@top fo
R5: {4dc 3ch 4dc}@sp [2ch 4sk sc@sp 2ch 4sk {4dc 3ch 4dc}@sp]x3 2ch 4sk sc@sp 2ch 4sk ss@top
R6: turn {3ch=dc 2dc}@sp [ch sk 3dc@sp ch 4sk {3dc 2ch 3dc}@sp ch 4sk 3dc@sp]x3 ch sk 3dc@sp ch 4sk {3dc 2ch 3dc}@sp ch 4sk ss@top # text says the bracket is worked 2 times, but the stated 16 shells / 4 corners need 3
R7: turn {3ch=dc ch dc}@sp [ch {vs 2ch vs}@sp [ch sk vs@sp]x3]x3 ch {vs 2ch vs}@sp [ch sk vs@sp]x2 ch ss@top fo
R8: vs@sp [ch sk vs@sp]x3 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp [[ch sk vs@sp]x4 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp]x3 ch sk ss@top
R9: turn {3ch=dc ch dc}@sp [ch sk vs@sp]x4 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp [[ch sk vs@sp]x5 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp]x3 ch sk ss@top
R10: turn {3ch=dc ch dc}@sp [ch sk vs@sp]x5 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp [[ch sk vs@sp]x6 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp]x3 ch sk ss@top fo
R11: vs@sp [ch sk vs@sp]x6 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp [[ch sk vs@sp]x7 ch sk {vs 2ch vs}@sp]x3 ch sk ss@top
R12: turn ch sc@sp [ch sk sc@sp]x16 ch sk {sc 2ch sc}@sp [[ch sk sc@sp]x17 ch sk {sc 2ch sc}@sp]x3 ch ss@top turn
R13-14: ch sc@same [[sc]>corner {sc 2ch sc}@sp]x4 [sc]>end ss@top
